    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d501">

                <pb facs="0571" n="469" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg469"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">417.00/282: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Nicaragua</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Munro</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-11-30T12:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 30,
                                1927—noon</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>210. Your 330, November 12, 11 a.m. Ascertain whether Claims Commission will pass
                    on the claim of Charles Butters for any damages which may have been caused to
                    the San Albino Mine by bandits in Nueva Segovia subsequent to June 30
                        last.<anchor n="68" xml:id="d501-f1"/> Report by telegraph.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d501-f1" n="68" xml:id="d501-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 161, June 30, 1927, 2 p.m., from the Minister in Nicaragua, <ref
                        target="#pg439">p. 439</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
